#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-system: what Hearth Settings' Date & time, Keyboard, Default apps, Users and Printers pages read and
change as you (no root). The parts that need root go through /usr/libexec/nimbus/hearth-admin (pkexec).

  hearth-system time                 JSON: time zone, automatic time, whether it's synced, the time now
  hearth-system timezones            JSON: every time zone as {zone, region, city, offset}
  hearth-system keyboard             JSON: your layouts (in order), the switch shortcut, repeat delay and rate
  hearth-system keyboard-layouts     JSON: every keyboard layout and variant the system knows
  hearth-system keyboard-set         stdin: {"layouts": [{"layout", "variant"}], "switch": "grp:...", "delay": ms,
                                     "rate": per second}. Writes ~/.config/labwc/environment (XKB_DEFAULT_*) and
                                     ~/.config/nimbus/keyboard.json, then asks labwc to reload
  hearth-system pointer              JSON: mouse and touchpad settings (speed, natural scrolling, tap to click...)
                                     and whether there's a touchpad
  hearth-system pointer-set          stdin: {"mouse": {...}, "touchpad": {...}} (see POINTER_KEYS). Writes
                                     ~/.config/nimbus/pointer.json, then asks labwc to reload
  hearth-system labwc-config         prepare Desktop Mode's labwc folder with your keyboard and mouse settings in it
                                     ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth-labwc) and print its path (nimbus-session runs it)
  hearth-system shortcuts            JSON: Desktop Mode's keyboard shortcuts, from labwc's rc.xml
  hearth-system defaults             JSON: the default browser, file manager, text editor, image viewer, video and
                                     music player, and the installed apps that can be each
  hearth-system default-set KIND APP_ID
                                     make APP_ID (a .desktop id) the default for KIND (mimeapps.list)
  hearth-system users                JSON: the accounts on this device, which one is you, who's an administrator
  hearth-system pictures             JSON: pictures you could use for your account
  hearth-system picture-set PATH|""  use a picture (PNG or JPEG) for your account ("" removes it)
  hearth-system printers             JSON: the printers (lpstat), which is the default, and their state
  hearth-system printer-test NAME    print a test page
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
